<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Fixlet>
    <Title>CentOS Firewall is Blocking BES Traffic - BES Client</Title>
    <Description><![CDATA[<TABLE>
<TBODY>
<TR>
<TD>
<P>The listed computers have iptables enabled and are not configured to allow inbound UDP traffic on the port used by BES (BES uses port 52311 by default). </P>
<P>The BES Server and BES Relays send UDP packets to the BES Clients to notify them that there is new information available such as new Fixlet messages, actions, and computer refreshes. BES Clients on relevant computers will not receive UDP notification packets and therefore will not see new actions or new Fixlet messages until they gather the new actionsite, which is by default, once a day. After configuring iptables to allow inbound UDP traffic on the BES Listen Port, BES Clients will resume normal communication with the BES Server and BES Relays.</P>
<P><FONT size=2><STRONG>Note:</STRONG> </FONT>After this action is applied, affected BES Clients will not report until they have performed their standard once-per-day gather or until the BES Client is restarted. </P>
<P><FONT size=2><STRONG>Note:</STRONG> The iptables firewall configuration is modified by inserting a new rule into the first position in the chain. Rules added after this fixlet is applied which try to take the first position in the firewall rules chain can override the&nbsp;rule added by this fixlet.</FONT></P>
<P><FONT size=2><STRONG><FONT color=#ff0000>Important Note:</FONT></STRONG> IPTables on systems running SELinux may fail to restart after running this fixlet.</FONT></P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>]]></Description>
    <Relevance>(if exists property &quot;in proxy agent context&quot; then ( not in proxy agent context ) else true )</Relevance>
    <Relevance><![CDATA[version of client >= "6"]]></Relevance>
    <Relevance><![CDATA[(if (version of client >= "8.0") then (unix of it) else ((it does not start with "Win" AND it does not start with "Mac OS X") of name of it)) of operating system]]></Relevance>
    <Relevance>exists file &quot;/var/lock/subsys/iptables&quot; AND exists file &quot;/proc/net/ip_tables_names&quot;</Relevance>
    <Relevance><![CDATA[version of client >= "7.2"]]></Relevance>
    <Relevance>exists match (regex &quot;Linux CentOS (3|4|5|6)&quot;) of name of operating system</Relevance>
    <Relevance><![CDATA[NOT exists file "/etc/sysconfig/iptables" whose (exists (lines of it) whose (it does not start with "#" AND exists match (regex ("--(destination-port|dport)s? +" & (port number of selected server as string))) of it AND it contains "-j ACCEPT")) AND exists file "/etc/sysconfig/iptables"]]></Relevance>
    <Category>Support</Category>
    <Source>BigFix</Source>
    <SourceID>&lt;Unspecified&gt;</SourceID>
    <SourceReleaseDate>2009-06-16</SourceReleaseDate>
    <SourceSeverity>Important</SourceSeverity>
    <MIMEField>
      <Name>x-fixlet-first-propagation</Name>
      <Value>Wed, 17 Jun 2009 18:18:35 +0000</Value>
    </MIMEField>
    <MIMEField>
      <Name>x-fixlet-domain_attributes</Name>
      <Value>BES Warn Important</Value>
    </MIMEField>
    <MIMEField>
      <Name>x-fixlet-modification-time</Name>
      <Value>Wed, 25 Feb 2015 15:06:51 +0000</Value>
    </MIMEField>
    <Domain>BESC</Domain>
    <DefaultAction ID="Action1">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink> to leave iptables enabled, but also allow incoming traffic on the port reserved for BES.</PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell"><![CDATA[//Modify the iptables saved ruleset
delete __appendfile

appendfile #!/bin/bash
appendfile sed -i -n '1h;1!H;${{;g;s/*filter\n\(:[^\n]*\n\)*/&-A INPUT -m state --state NEW -m udp -p udp --dport {port number of selected server as string} -j ACCEPT\n/g;p;}' /etc/sysconfig/iptables
appendfile /etc/init.d/iptables restart

wait chmod +x "{(client folder of current site as string) & "/__appendfile"}"

wait "{(client folder of current site as string) & "/__appendfile"}"

//delete delete __appendfile]]></ActionScript>
    </DefaultAction>
    <Action ID="Action4434">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink> to disable iptables firewall.</PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell"><![CDATA[//Disable iptables
delete __appendfile

appendfile #!/bin/bash
appendfile chkconfig --level 2345 iptables off
appendfile /etc/init.d/iptables stop

wait chmod +x "{(client folder of current site as string) & "/__appendfile"}"

wait "{(client folder of current site as string) & "/__appendfile"}"

//delete delete __appendfile]]></ActionScript>
    </Action>
    <Action ID="Action4435">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink> for information on how to make this action a &quot;policy&quot; action that will automatically open the BES port on any computer that has this Fixlet message relevant. </PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="text/x-uri">http://support.bigfix.com/cgi-bin/kbdirect.pl?id=113</ActionScript>
    </Action>
  </Fixlet>
</BES>
